{"full":"json-ld/json-ld.org","name":"json-ld.org","description":"JSON for Linked Data's documentation and playground site","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":921,"forks":165,"created":"2011-05-27T01:36:23Z","updated":"2026-06-17T20:01:40Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://json-ld.org/","topics":["api","json","json-ld","web"],"demo":"https://json-ld.org/playground/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:32.237Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:32.237Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:32.237Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:25:27.543Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:10.335Z","stars":921,"forks":165},{"at":"2026-10-04T05:48:32.237Z","stars":921,"forks":165}],"technologies":[],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:06:37.567Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["JSON-LD (JavaScript Object Notation for Linking Data) is a lightweight Linked Data format. It is easy for humans to read and write. It is easy for machines to parse and generate. It is based on the already successful JSON format and provides a way to help JSON data interoperate at Web-scale. If you are already familiar with JSON, writing JSON-LD is very easy. There is a smooth migration path from the JSON you use today, to the JSON-LD you will use in the future. These properties make JSON-LD an ideal Linked Data interchange language for JavaScript environments, Web services, and unstructured…","If you are already using JSON-LD, add yourself to the list of users in our wiki."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/json-ld/json-ld.org/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"52a3176371ee32e4d428da7de92e07e7b01c4e47970c913fa697f0fe66a4726c","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:28:06.869Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:06:42.643Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-17T20:01:40Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"JSON-LD (JavaScript Object Notation for Linking Data) is a lightwe